fourth of july celebrations in a north  las vegas neighborhood turned  deadly two men are dead and others are  injured after a shooting late last night  this happened on helen avenue near cary  and martin luther king boulevard  kate houston spoke to neighbors who say  the escalation of violence  is worrying the community  here you can see police tape is still up  from last night's shooting one neighbor  tells me that the fireworks were so loud  last night they couldn't even hear  gunshots  after hours of fourth of july  celebrations police were called to the  neighborhood just after 11.  neighbors say they saw a swarm of police  cars and a crowd of people running from  parties  north las vegas police say seven people  were injured and two men believed to be  in their early 20's  died nicholas powell and lila hampton  say this is a tight community  and while they've had shootings and  drive-bys before nothing compares to  this  for me the sad part is knowing that  there's other families out there that  are going to wake up and realize  that their family member is not coming  home this is tragedy  every time you turn around someone is  getting killed or something somewhere  monday afternoon detectives were  canvassing the block which was filled  with used fireworks and party cups  they're pursuing all leads anyone with  information is asked to call the north  las vegas police department  kate houston 8 news now
 

